{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I cried out and you [Ab]heard the sound
[Eb]My pleading reached your [Ab]gentle ear
[Eb]You answered when I [Cm]was bound
And drove away all my fear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]The Lord is my strength and my shield
In him [Bb]my heart trusted [Cm]deep
I was helped [Ab]and my heart [Eb]leaped
With joy [Bb]and songs I will [Cm]keep
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You [Ab]do not tear me [Eb]down
You build me [Ab]up to stand
[Eb]In your hands [Ab]I am found
[Eb]Grasping [Cm]your steady hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The Lord is [Ab]my strength and my shield
In him my [Bb]heart trusted [Cm]deep
I was helped [Ab]and my heart [Eb]leaped
With joy [Bb]and songs I will [Cm]keep
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
You are the [Ab]saving strong[Eb]hold
[Ab]For the anointed you [Bb]hold
[Cm]Bless your inheritance and [Ebmaj7/G]make [Ab]whole
Carry us forev[Bb]er old
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Cm7]The Lord is my strength [Ab]and my shield
In him my [Bb]heart trusted [Cm7]deep
I was helped [Ab]and my heart [Eb]leaped
With joy [Bb]and songs I will [Cm7]keep
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
